+						// dsh-manage patch (2026-08-28): the explicit-model path
+						// (modelResolver.resolve's first branch) returns
+						// { model } with NO provider key. Building agentOptions
+						// with `provider: task.model.provider` here always makes
+						// that key EXIST as an explicit `undefined`, which
+						// resolveChildAgentOptions() in @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent
+						// spreads verbatim (`...requested`), overwriting the
+						// inherited parent provider with undefined instead of
+						// leaving it untouched -- the child then starts with no
+						// route. Omitting the key entirely when there is no
+						// provider (same defensive pattern the harness itself
+						// uses elsewhere) lets the spread fall through to the
+						// parent's provider as intended. Root cause reported
+						// upstream: hongyue0721/dsh-kimicode-swarm.
 						agentOptions: task.model === void 0 ? void 0 : {
-							provider: task.model.provider,
